// parts of operating system :
1) shell 
2) kernel

1) shell :
--> a interface which abstracts the kernel and functionality of operating system (OS)

2) kernel :
--> which contains functionality of os to interact with the user and contains hardware of the operating system (OS)

// interfaces :
1) GUI
2) CLI

1) GUI : graphical user interface which is used to interact with the computer .
2) CLI : command line interface which is used to interact with the kernel . 

// Modes of the operating system :
1) User mode 
2) Dual mode 

1) User mode : user mode has very non priviliged access means he cant access to the kernel and change the functionality of the operating system ( mode bit == 1 ) . 
2) Dual mode : dual mode is the kernel mode which has access and it can be accessed by getting the priviliged access ( modebit == 0 ) .

// dual mode is used to access protection and security . 
